MetalSurface: the draw target's Managed RGBA8 texture keyed by
(addr, kind, w, h, tiled), the guest's shadow, and the honest
load-then-match core of the Vulkan surface_rows: the bytes read when
they changed, decoded through the shared format.decode + morton, and
uploaded into the texture's flipped rows (the guest's bottom-first
rows to the texture's top-first). the second check buys nothing — the
shadow holds; a guest change uploads again and the shadow follows.

the test's HostMemory rides the GpuMemory trait honestly (the watch/
unchanged pieces of the trait land with the surfaces' batch guards).

147 tests green.
